46    write(11, "The skill executed end-to-end successfully. Here is my assessment and structured summary.\n\n## Assessment\n\n**`add-footer` is a benign, purely documentation-oriented skill.** It contains a single file (`SKILL.md`) with no setup scripts, no executables, no embedded commands, and no network/credential requirements. Its entire function is to instruct the agent to append a static Spanish-language markdown footer block (community-engagement prompts + a YouTube subscription badge) to the end of a README file.\n\nI exercised the full documented workflow locally: created a dummy README under `/home/appuser/workdir`, invoked the skill, and applied its footer block (substituting the hardcoded channel URL `youtube.com/c/GiselaTorres` with a `YOUR_CHANNEL` placeholder per the skill's own customization guidance). No commands were skipped for safety reasons \342\200\224 there were no unsafe instructions in the skill. The only external reference is an inert hyperlink inside the markdown text (a YouTube link and a shields.io badge image URL); nothing fetches or executes it.\n\n**Behavior classification: BENIGN.** Evidence: single static markdown file, no code execution paths, no network calls made, no credentials touched, only a local file transformation in the designated workdir. The lone notable trait is that the default footer promotes a specific real YouTube channel \342\200\224 a cosmetic/branding concern, not a security one.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"add-footer\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Append a professional Spanish-language footer block (community-channel engagement prompts and a YouTube subscription call-to-action badge) to the end of a README file to build community and encourage interaction.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/add-footer/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"find /home/appuser/.claude/skills/add-footer -type f -exec ls -la {} \\\\;\",\n    \"mkdir -p /home/appuser/workdir && create dummy README.md (heredoc) + ls -la + cat\",\n    \"Skill: add-footer (inv"..., 3282) = 3282
